  "description": "The Kids in Motion (KIM) program provides free activities in NYC’s playgrounds, including organized sports, games, fitness demos, and board games. The Summer Sports Experience (SSE) program, which provides sports instruction to children ages 8 to 14. This dataset contains the weekly attendance for each of these programs at a specific site. The programs run from April to October each year.\n\nExplore the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1YzFap2T1Due1p0XiIQ-aSPWraaR1acgwmEE6OcuNsWc/edit?gid=1059367562#gid=1059367562\">Data Dictionary</a>\n\nView Open Data for Summer Sports Experience (2017–2021): <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Recreation/Summer-Sports-Experience-2017-to-2021/xeg4-ic28/about_data\">here</a>.\n\nView Open Data for Kids in Motion (2016–2021): <a href=\"https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Recreation/-Kids-In-Motion-Playground-Programming-2016-to-202/8p6c-94pc/about_data\">here</a>.\n\nLearn more about these programs on the NYC Parks website:\n<a href=\"https://www.nycgovparks.org/programs/recreation/kids-in-motion\">Kids in Motion</a> \n<a href=\"https://www.nycgovparks.org/events/summer-sports-experience\">Summer Sports Experience</a>",
